Resolve the repository root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` and run all commands from there.

Deploy only after the pull request is merged. Require local `main` to be clean and exactly match `origin/main`, then run `npm run prod:deploy`.

The deploy command owns the immutable image build, SQLite/uploads backup, health-checked cutover, release manifest, and automatic rollback. Do not copy source into a second production checkout and do not run a separate snapshot command.

Never print, archive, or commit production paths, environment files, credentials, tailnet identifiers, database contents, uploads, or other private machine data.
